' 18. Customize the traveller (wardrobe)
' Use case: Customize traveller (Manage account) · Actor: Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Repository: traveller-look.repository.ts (one row per learner, saved with an upsert)
'   - Observer (web): the look is a useSyncExternalStore store (nihon-web/src/lib/useTravellerLook.ts), so every
'     traveller on screen (island map, village, wild paths, battles) redraws when it changes
'   - Validation at the boundary: every part must be one of its choices (traveller.service.ts parseLook → 400)
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens, «control» use-case logic, «entity» stored data; the database
' keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 18 Customize the traveller
title 18. Customize the traveller (wardrobe)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app\n(wardrobe)" as Web
entity "Traveller look store\n(browser)" as Store
control "Traveller controller" as Ctrl
control "Traveller service" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB

note over Web, Ctrl : «Chain of responsibility»: headers → CORS → authenticate → controller\n«Decorator»: action() wraps every controller (error handling)

Learner -> Web : Open "Dress your traveller" (from the profile)
Web -> Store : read the saved look
alt not kept in this browser yet
  Web -> Ctrl : GET /api/traveller/look
  Ctrl -> Svc : getTravellerLook()
  Svc -> Repo : findTravellerLook()
  Repo -> DB : SELECT … FROM traveller_looks
  Svc --> Ctrl : the look, or the default one
  Ctrl --> Web : look
  Web -> Store : remember the look
end
Web -> Web : show the preview and a choice for each part

loop trying things on
  Learner -> Web : Choose kimono / skin / sash / hair / hat / carrying / cheeks
  Web -> Web : redraw the preview at once (draft only, nothing sent)
end
opt see it move
  Learner -> Web : Walk
  Web -> Web : preview walks
end

alt Save
  Learner -> Web : Save
  Web -> Ctrl : PUT /api/traveller/look { outfit, sash, skin, hair, hat, accessory, cheeks }
  Ctrl -> Svc : saveTravellerLook(body)
  Svc -> Svc : parseLook(): every part one of its choices?
  alt a part is missing or unknown
    Svc --> Web : 400 "Choose one of the … options."
    Web -> Web : show "Could not save your traveller. Please try again.", keep the draft
  else valid
    Svc -> Repo : saveTravellerLook()
    Repo -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT (user_id) DO UPDATE
    Svc --> Ctrl : look
    Ctrl --> Web : look
    Web -> Store : remember the look
    Store -> Web : every traveller on screen redraws
    note right of Store : «Observer»\nsubscribed components\nupdate together
    Web -> Web : show "Saved. Your traveller wears it everywhere now."
  end
else Back to the first look
  Learner -> Web : Back to the first look
  Web -> Web : draft = default look (Save still needed)
end
@enduml
